    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1163">

                <pb facs="1360" n="1162" xml:id="pg1162"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">London Embassy Files—870 EITO</note>
                <head>No. 1163<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The British Acting Assistant
                        Under-Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Ronald</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Minister in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hawkins</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extracts]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">W 10212/22/13</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-08-03">August 3, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Hawkins</hi>, After you left me yesterday I …
                    addressed a telegram to our Chargé d’Affaires in Warsaw<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1163-f1"/> in the terms of the enclosed. …<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d1163-f2"/></p>
                <p>You will notice that I adopted your suggestion that we should mention an actual
                    date in our communication. I was all the more inclined to do this when I heard
                    from Weston that the Soviet Delegation at <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Terminal</hi> had definitely favoured quick progress in this field.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Nigel Ronald</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d1163-a1.xml" xpointer="d1163-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1163-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1163-f1-content">
                <p>Hon. Robert M. A. Hankey.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1163-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1163-f2-content">
                <p>Instructing the Chargé to invite the Polish Provisional Government to send a
                    delegation to the European Inland Transport Conference.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
